---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/sequenzy-vs-privy';
const title = "Sequenzy vs Privy for Shopify email";
const desc = "Evaluate the signup experience and downstream data handoff before buying a second platform.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Must I use Privy and Sequenzy together?",
    "answer": "No. First identify a requirement the existing configuration cannot meet. Both advertise email automation, and Sequenzy also advertises forms."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify contact sync prove the welcome handoff works?",
    "answer": "No. Inspect permission, signup source and offer fields in the receiving account and test the actual trigger."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
<header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Privy for Shopify email</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Evaluate the signup experience and downstream data handoff before buying a second platform.</p></header>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Privy is also an email platform</h2>
<p>Privy lists email and SMS campaigns, automations, segmentation and reporting alongside its popup products. Calling it a capture tool with no meaningful retention capability would misrepresent that scope. Its email pricing uses mailable contacts and unlimited sends; its displays-only product uses monthly page views. Those are separate purchase decisions, not one combined traffic-and-contact charge.</p>
<h2>Decide whether capture or follow-up is broken</h2>
<p>For a proposed candle launch, inspect the journey from a mobile product page to signup, coupon receipt and first purchase. If the signup form fails, replacing the email sender alone will not repair it. If subscribers arrive but receive the wrong offer, inspect the automation and data first. Sequenzy also advertises forms and popups, so keeping Privy is a choice to validate rather than an automatic prerequisite.</p>
<h2>Make the offer handoff explicit</h2>
<p>Create internal signups through a standard popup, a spin-to-win offer and an embedded form. Record the promised incentive, signup source and permission state. Privy documents Shopify contact sync, but that does not prove all campaign properties reach Sequenzy or start the intended branch. Inspect both records. If the source field is missing, use a verified mapping or a simpler welcome; do not silently send an incompatible coupon.</p>
<h2>Rehearse existing subscribers and withdrawals</h2>
<p>Submit the form with an address already subscribed, an address previously unsubscribed and a customer who buys before the welcome delay ends. Check whether any new offer is promised, whether permission changes, and whether the welcome repeats. Test withdrawal propagation in both directions if two services remain. A contact existing in Shopify is not evidence of permission for every channel.</p>
<h2>Use a second platform only for an identified gap</h2>
<p>Write the exact unmet follow-up requirement, such as branching by a reliably supplied signup source or excluding a recent purchaser. Attempt it in the existing Privy account, then in Sequenzy using the same test inputs. Save the actual event records and operator steps. There is no defensible contact-count or monthly-order threshold at which every merchant must add Sequenzy. A working single-service journey can be preferable to maintaining a handoff.</p>
<h2>Price the configuration you will keep</h2>
<p>Compare Privy email alone, Privy displays plus Sequenzy email, and Sequenzy alone if its capture experience meets the brief. Use mailable contacts for Privy email, page views for displays and email volume for Sequenzy. Add SMS and integration work only when included in the plan. Measure completed purchases and offer cost alongside signup rate; a higher capture rate alone does not establish profitable retention. Keep Privy if its complete journey meets the need; split ownership only when a demonstrated benefit covers the extra work.</p>
<h2>Sources and scope</h2>
<p>Checked November 25, 2026. Vendor documentation establishes advertised scope, not tested account behavior. Exercises above are proposed, not completed merchant tests.</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/pricing">Privy email and displays pricing</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy feature and channel scope</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/sequenzy">Sequenzy Shopify listing</a></li>
</ul>
</article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-omnisend">Sequenzy vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-shopify-email">Sequenzy vs Shopify Email</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions before choosing" />
</BaseLayout>
